### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### VALIDACIONES Y CASOS DE ERROR
###
### Pre-requisito: tener creados los users "test" (ADMIN) y "userb" (USER).
### Ejecuta primero los Logins de abajo para capturar tokens.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@host = http://localhost:8080
@apiV1 = {{host}}/api/v1


### Login admin → token en {{tokenAdmin}}
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}

> {%
client.global.set("tokenAdmin", response.body.token);
%}


### Login user → token en {{tokenUser}}
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "userb@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}

> {%
client.global.set("tokenUser", response.body.token);
%}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### AUTH — errores
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


### 401 — Login con password incorrecta
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@test.com",
  "password": "passwordmal"
}


### 401 — Login con email que no existe (mismo mensaje, no filtramos info)
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "noexiste@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}


### 409 — Register con email ya registrado
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "otro",
  "email": "test@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}


### 409 — Register con username ya registrado
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "test",
  "email": "diferente@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}


### 400 — Register con varios campos mal
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "x",
  "email": "no-es-email",
  "password": "12"
}


### 400 — Register con body vacío
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### USERS — errores
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


### 401 — sin token
GET {{apiV1}}/users/me


### 401 — token inválido
GET {{apiV1}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer chorizo-no-valido


### 401 — header sin "Bearer "
GET {{apiV1}}/users/me
Authorization: {{tokenUser}}


### 403 — USER intenta listar todos los users
GET {{apiV1}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenUser}}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### CONTAINERS — errores
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


### 400 — Crear sin imagen (falla validación @NotBlank)
POST {{apiV1}}/containers
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "sin-imagen",
  "autoStart": true
}


### 400 — Crear con body totalmente vacío
POST {{apiV1}}/containers
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}


### 401 — Listar sin token
GET {{apiV1}}/containers


### 500 — Crear con imagen inexistente (Docker no la encuentra)
POST {{apiV1}}/containers
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "image": "imagen-que-no-existe:99",
  "autoStat": true
}


### Pre-paso para errores 403: admin crea un container y guardamos su id
### (después userb intentará tocarlo)
POST {{apiV1}}/containers
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "image": "nginx:alpine",
  "name": "admin-protegido",
  "autoStart": true
}

> {%
client.global.set("adminContainerId", response.body.id);
%}


### 403 — userb intenta inspeccionar container de admin
GET {{apiV1}}/containers/{{adminContainerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenUser}}


### 403 — userb intenta parar container de admin
POST {{apiV1}}/containers/{{adminContainerId}}/stop
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenUser}}


### 403 — userb intenta borrar container de admin
DELETE {{apiV1}}/containers/{{adminContainerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenUser}}


### 403 — userb intenta ver logs de container de admin
GET {{apiV1}}/containers/{{adminContainerId}}/logs
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenUser}}


### Limpieza: admin borra el container que creó arriba
DELETE {{apiV1}}/containers/{{adminContainerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}


### 500 — Operar sobre container que no existe (Docker lo rechaza)
GET {{apiV1}}/containers/no-existe-este-id
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
